    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the policy side, but you're framing it like the \"managed risks\" are easy to handle, when for an investor, \"messy\" usually means massive volatility and capital loss. it feels like you're dismissing the possibility that the transition could stall out or fail to meet these timelines due to sheer economic reality. are you saying that the climate/regulatory argument effectively outweighs all traditional macroeconomic and engineering constraints?",
