      "content": "You are correct that the transition will be messy and volatile, but the sheer scale of global policy mandates and public demand makes a total stall-out statistically improbable. While engineering constraints exist, they are being solved faster than the fossil fuel industry can pivot, meaning the regulatory pressure will eventually force a resolution regardless of current economic friction. For an investor, the real risk isn't the transition failing, but the catastrophic financial loss of holding assets that become obsolete before they can be sold.",
